Z||000011||LZeitgeist||08-24-2001||03:04 PM||||The 'Turbo Interceptor' used in 'The Wraith' was actually the Dodge/Chrysler-built PPG (Pittsburgh Paint & Glass) Pace Car. There were six copies of the car that were built for the movie. The car was rear-wheel-drive, power by a 2.2L Cosworth twin-intercooled-turbocharged dohc in-line four putting out a supposed 440 horsepower, and the original car cost $1.5 million.<P>For further information, check out this website: <A HREF="http://www.auto-enthusiast.com/ShelbyDodge/Wraith/index.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.auto-enthusiast.com/ShelbyDodge/Wraith/index.htm</A> <P><P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001||||reg||1
